      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fe2O3 or CoFe2O4 can serve as a hard magnetic secondary phase in this system.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidation at 300–500 °C in air or oxygen can produce sub-micron or nanoscale oxide precipitates while retaining a majority fcc matrix.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting oxide precipitates will be embedded in the fcc FeCoNi matrix.",
